WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:03.769
-Hey.

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:06.806
Hey, up here.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.476
Hi, I'm Jimmy Fallon.
Welcome to another edition

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.911
of "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.613
I'm up in a tree.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.448
Paper comes from trees.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:20.352
Written on this paper
is redcross.org/statefarm.

00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:22.788
Our good neighbors
at State Farm decided

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:28.160
that they would match up to
$100,000 in donations this week.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.962
So please donate to that.

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:32.665
In fact, in just two days

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.568
I got to say it's working
and in a big way,

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.004
and it's really cool and
really important and really fun,

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:40.840
so that State Farm
got very excited and called us

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.309
and said they're actually
going to double that.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.211
That's how well it's going.
So it's working, guys.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.446
So thank you so much.
This is awesome.

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:52.017
Up to $200,000 they're
going to match this week.

00:00:52.017 --> 00:00:53.419
So please donate to that.

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:55.788
It is working.
What you're doing is great.

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:57.290
Thank you. Thank you so much.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.125
We have a great show tonight.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:02.261
Former Vice President Joe Biden
is on our show tonight.

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:05.431
We're gonna be talking about
coronavirus,

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:09.102
the election, how coronavirus
has affected the election.

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:11.804
And there's so many --
so much stuff

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:13.072
we have to talk about tonight.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:15.575
Also, I'll be talking
with Lady Gaga,

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.076
who has a giant announcement

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:19.045
that she wants to make tonight
on our show.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.346
We appreciate that.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:24.717
And we'll be talking
to Andy Puddicombe, who is...

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:29.789
[Quietly] the owner
and very calm -- very calm voice

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:32.859
that you hear
when you have Headspace app.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.594
He's whispering in your ear.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:35.728
[ Normal voice ]
That's the voice.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.664
Andy is on the show tonight,
going to tell us

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:39.399
about meditation
and why it's important,

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.133
and is it hard? Is it easy?

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:44.804
How we can do it? Breathing.
How to deal with anxiety.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.105
We'll be talking with him.

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:47.640
And then we're going
to close the show tonight

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.409
with Marcus Mumford,
with a new song from him.

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:52.612
So thank you, Marcus.
We love you.

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:56.115
Guys, how about
we do a little monologue?

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:58.318
Need help getting up here?

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.020
Hey, guys,
before we start this monologue,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.289
I wanted to show you a really
cool video from Anna Higgins,

00:02:37.289 --> 00:02:40.026
who is Steve Higgins' daughter,
our announcer.

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:41.360
This is a video of her.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.830
She's a nurse
over at Mt. Sinai in Manhattan.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.332
And she goes to work every day.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.733
And she was walking to work

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:50.904
and decided to videotape
her walk to work.

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:53.072
Take a look at how cool this is.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:56.075
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:00.979 --> 00:03:03.449
-You can do it, New York!

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:09.322
-I love you, New York.
Stay strong.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:10.523
That is awesome.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:12.759
Guys, let's get to
the monologue. Here we go.

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:14.860
Welcome to "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition" monologue.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:18.130
This is very exciting.
Joe Biden is my guest tonight.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.333
He's actually pretty spry
for 77.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:23.403
For example, he's going to Zoom
with me tonight.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.271
That's right, Biden's been
campaigning from home,

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.638
but it's a little awkward.

00:03:26.638 --> 00:03:28.407
Every day, he shakes hands
with his wife, Jill,

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:31.810
and asks where she's from.
[ Chuckles ]

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:34.113
That's right, Biden has been
running for president from home.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.948
That's right.
It's just him, his family,

00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:39.385
and 10,000 Crest Whitestrips.

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:40.920
Well, guys,
today is U.S. Census Day.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.023
Yep, the census happens
once every 10 years

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:47.160
like a Batman reboot
or a Larry King marriage.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.728
Some sports news --
There's a chance

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:51.030
that the Tour de France
might get canceled.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.399
Not 'cause of the virus --
'cause after two months at home,

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:56.636
no one wants to be seen
in spandex.

00:03:56.636 --> 00:04:00.272
I saw that some neighbors are
communicating with window signs.

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:02.841
That's right, you can write "hi"
to your neighbor, "stay strong,"

00:04:02.841 --> 00:04:04.610
or "Why did you park
in front of my house

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:08.213
when there's a spot
in front of yours?"

00:04:08.213 --> 00:04:10.216
Meanwhile, some adults
are turning to coloring books

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.184
as a way to relieve stress.

00:04:12.184 --> 00:04:14.787
Yep, it relieves stress
right up until your kids realize

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:17.523
someone's filled in
all their coloring books.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:19.425
"Mom!"

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.826
Some entertainment news --

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:24.096
Christopher Maloney will reprise
his "Law &amp; Order" character,

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:26.665
Elliot Stabler,
in a new spin-off series.

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:28.134
Even though it's not
"Law &amp; Order,"

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:30.269
somehow Ice-T
will show up in every scene

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:34.507
to say, "Guess we better
pay him a visit."

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:37.343
And now fans of movie "Little
Women" have found a water bottle

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:40.113
and a hydroflask
in the background of a scene.

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.614
Unfortunately,
once you notice the flub,

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.482
it really ruins the scene
that takes place

00:04:43.482 --> 00:04:46.218
at a Buffalo Wild Wings.

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:48.721
And finally, over 4,000 pounds
of drugs were found

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.923
in a tunnel near San Diego.

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.425
The drugs have a street value
of $30 million,

00:04:53.425 --> 00:04:56.728
or roughly one full
package of Charmin.

00:04:56.728 --> 00:04:58.397
And that's tonight's monologue.

00:04:58.397 --> 00:04:59.932
Thank you very much, everybody.

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.602
Well, we wanted to check in
with our pal, Lady Gaga.

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:05.504
She has some big news she wanted
to talk to me about today.

00:05:05.504 --> 00:05:08.274
So I got to FaceTime with her.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:10.609
Connecting.

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:13.646
Yeah. Hi. Lady Gaga?

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.514
-Hi. Hi, everyone.

00:05:15.514 --> 00:05:17.983
-We have a big
maybe announcement

00:05:17.983 --> 00:05:20.386
that you're going to say tonight
on our show?

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.721
-I can't, Jimmy.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.889
I can't talk right now.

00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:26.191
I'm really sorry.

00:05:26.191 --> 00:05:29.128
It's just, like,
a really weird time --

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:30.496
Hello?
-Yeah.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.165
-Jimmy? I can't see you.
-You're on --

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:34.099
-Am I on TV?

00:05:34.099 --> 00:05:35.501
-Yeah.
-Hold on.

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:38.571
-Sorry. You're on TV.
I apologize.

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:40.139
[ Phone ringing ]

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:42.274
Wait, what's --
-Wait. Hold on.

00:05:42.274 --> 00:05:43.709
-What's the big news?

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:45.311
[ Phone ringing ]

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:48.714
-Hey, guys, can you push that
call back one minute, please?

00:05:48.714 --> 00:05:50.048
-Yep, okay.

00:05:50.048 --> 00:05:52.618
-There's something that
you're working on, very big,

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:56.421
that's going to
help people out right now.

00:05:56.421 --> 00:05:58.691
-I can't -- I can't --

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:01.260
I can't tell you everything
right now,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:05.331
because I'm still
ironing out the details.

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:07.866
And I have
a lot of phone calls today.

00:06:07.866 --> 00:06:10.536
-Do you want me
to call you back?

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:14.206
What's a good time,
like 10 minutes?

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:17.977
-Can you call me --
Can you call me Friday?

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:20.379
-Can I call you on Friday?
-Yeah.

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:23.249
-[ Laughs ] It's --

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:24.317
Yeah. It's --

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:25.351
-Am I on TV?

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:26.919
-It's Wednesday.

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:29.722
-Can I call Fallon on Friday?

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.690
Okay, thank you.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.627
Friday's great.
I can do Friday.

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.228
-Okay, I'll do Friday.
I'll talk to you --

00:06:36.228 --> 00:06:39.565
-It's for COVID-19.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:42.801
-Okay. Alright.
I'll call you on Friday.

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:44.570
-Bye. Love you.
-Bye, pal. I love you, too.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.772
-I'm so sorry I can't talk right
now. I'm so sorry.

00:06:46.772 --> 00:06:48.841
I just -- I want to get --

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.176
I'm trying --

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:51.743
-If it's big,
we'll make sure it's --

00:06:51.743 --> 00:06:52.811
Okay, alright, here we go.

00:06:52.811 --> 00:06:55.013
Alright.
I'll call you on Friday.

00:06:55.013 --> 00:06:57.917
Okay. So I guess
I won't be talking to her

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.452
about the big news until Friday.

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:00.620
So we have until Friday

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:03.822
to guess what the big news
is going to be.

00:07:03.822 --> 00:07:05.992
Oh, wait, she called me back.

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:07.760
Hello?

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.461
-I'm sorry, I just have to --

00:07:09.461 --> 00:07:12.698
Can we just move our time?

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:14.700
-Yeah, you want me to move it?

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.535
-Yeah, I -- Can we do it Monday?

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:19.071
I promise we'll do it Monday.

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:22.841
-You want to wait till Monday.
Today's Wednesday, so --

00:07:22.841 --> 00:07:24.410
Monday?
[ Laughs ]

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.611
[ Phone ringing ]

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:28.014
Oh, my heavens,
you are the busiest person!

00:07:28.014 --> 00:07:30.483
[ Laughing ]

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:32.318
So I guess it's Monday.

00:07:32.318 --> 00:07:36.154
Monday is when we'll find out
the big news from Lady Gaga.

00:07:36.154 --> 00:07:38.457
Not today, Wednesday, no.

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:40.960
Not Friday, nope.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.796
Next Monday is when we'll find
out the big news from Lady Gaga.

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:47.099
Thank you, Gaga,
and I cannot wait to find out

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:48.834
what you're brewing.
It's going to be fun.

00:07:48.834 --> 00:07:51.037
Guys, right now, it's my time --
It's Wednesday.

00:07:51.037 --> 00:07:53.606
It's time to show you
some of my favorite videos

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:56.408
that I've seen you guys make
in this quarantine.

00:07:56.408 --> 00:07:58.978
It's called
"What Are You Doing Wednesdays."

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:01.313
♪♪

00:08:01.313 --> 00:08:02.982
Alright, so, this is
"What Are You Doing Wednesdays."

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:04.816
We all know what you're doing.
You're staying at home,

00:08:04.816 --> 00:08:06.552
but these videos
all made me laugh.

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:09.187
This first one here
is a granddaughter

00:08:09.187 --> 00:08:12.458
and her grandfather
having a dance-off,

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:15.928
but distance -- socially
distancing dance-off.

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:17.529
Please enjoy.

00:08:17.529 --> 00:08:27.373
♪♪

00:08:27.373 --> 00:08:37.216
♪♪

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:39.818
Grandpa's got the moves.

00:08:39.818 --> 00:08:42.822
This next video
is a girl who wants to --

00:08:42.822 --> 00:08:44.423
She's tired of her boyfriend
playing games.

00:08:44.423 --> 00:08:46.225
He's gaming too much
during quarantine.

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:47.626
So she wanted him to stop.

00:08:47.626 --> 00:08:51.964
And this is her idea
of how to make him stop.

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:03.876
-Hey, babe.

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:06.412
[ Laughing ]

00:09:06.412 --> 00:09:08.747
Hold on, guys.
Alisha's on my shoulders.

00:09:08.747 --> 00:09:11.383
What's going -- Jesus Christ!

00:09:11.383 --> 00:09:14.219
-Our last one, this guy
misses swimming so much,

00:09:14.219 --> 00:09:16.788
but he thought of way around it
in this quarantine.

00:09:16.788 --> 00:09:19.958
Pretty ingenious. Check it out.

00:09:19.958 --> 00:09:23.029
-[ Gasps ]

00:09:23.029 --> 00:09:25.031
[ Gasping ]

00:09:36.475 --> 00:09:38.544
-That was
"What Are You Doing Wednesdays."

00:09:38.544 --> 00:09:41.046
Thank you so much for those.
Keep filming yourself

00:09:41.046 --> 00:09:43.749
doing all sorts of crazy stuff
during this quarantine.

00:09:43.749 --> 00:09:45.718
We'll be scouring the web
and picking our favorites.

